<Root>
  <DefaultMacro>
    <Major>Azure Latch</Major>
    <Description>This macro for the Azure Latch game in Roblox performs three actions sequentially. Before using it, be sure to activate auto-headder inside the games stettings for best and easy performance. The macro throws the ball and then performs a head kick. Next, he jumps and makes a dash for the ball, hitting it with his head again. This is followed by another headbutt. The original screen resolution is 1920 x 1080 (RECONMMENDED), while you should have 800 DPI (for better control) and 0.171 sensitivity in Roblox. To make the macro work correctly, hold down the W key during its execution, but release it for a short moment after the second headbutt so that the rest of the actions go smoothly. Have Fun.</Description>
    <Comment></Comment>
    <GUIOption>
      <RepeatType>0</RepeatType>
    </GUIOption>
    <KeyUp>
      <Syntax></Syntax>
    </KeyUp>
    <KeyDown>
      <Syntax>LeftDown 1
Delay 16 ms
LeftUp 1
Delay 16 ms
MoveR 0 855 1 875
Delay 8 ms
MoveR 0 855 1 875
Delay 275 ms
KeyDown 44 1
Delay 32 ms
KeyUp 44 1
Delay 768 ms
KeyDown 44 1
Delay 32 ms
KeyUp 44 1
KeyDown 20 1
KeyUp 20 1
Delay 768 ms
KeyDown 44 1
Delay 32 ms
KeyUp 44 1
Delay 120 ms
KeyDown 9 1
KeyUp 9 1</Syntax>
    </KeyDown>
    <Software>Roblox</Software>
  </DefaultMacro>
</Root>